  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "41159698",
      "title": "React Server Components vs Client Components - When To Use What",
      "lectureOrder": 104,
      "videoOrder": 97,
      "sourceHash": "d33898aee8a45dfa8251f5fbca8a62d856f1d150a14ad2bc5a60fb274f8a665b",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.6,
          "end": 1.65,
          "en": "Now that's something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 1.65,
          "end": 4.56,
          "en": "that's super important in NextJS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 4.56,
          "end": 7.74,
          "en": "NextJS knows Server components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 7.74,
          "end": 11.94,
          "en": "React Server components and Client Components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.94,
          "end": 16.59,
          "en": "And actually that's technically not just NextJS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.59,
          "end": 20.4,
          "en": "instead, React itself has this differentiation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.4,
          "end": 22.29,
          "en": "though in most React apps,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.29,
          "end": 24.36,
          "en": "in all those vanilla React apps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.36,
          "end": 27.24,
          "en": "which you are building with help of create React app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.24,
          "end": 28.92,
          "en": "or with help of Vite,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 28.92,
          "end": 32.7,
          "en": "you are using client components out of the box.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.7,
          "end": 34.44,
          "en": "Because in those projects,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 34.44,
          "end": 37.98,
          "en": "React.js is a pure client side library,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 37.98,
          "end": 41.79,
          "en": "running code in the browser on the client.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 41.79,
          "end": 43.95,
          "en": "With NextJS, that changes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 43.95,
          "end": 46.92,
          "en": "because NextJS is a full stack framework.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 46.92,
          "end": 50.19,
          "en": "It has a backend, not just a front end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 50.19,
          "end": 52.26,
          "en": "and therefore code also executes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 52.26,
          "end": 55.56,
          "en": "on that backend when working with NextJS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 55.56,
          "end": 59.37,
          "en": "And for example, by default, all those React components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 59.37,
          "end": 61.41,
          "en": "you have in your NextJS project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 61.41,
          "end": 65.61,
          "en": "no matter if they're pages, layouts or standard components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 65.61,
          "end": 68.94,
          "en": "are only rendered on the Server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 68.94,
          "end": 71.973,
          "en": "That's why they're called React Server components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 73.05,
          "end": 75.69,
          "en": "Now as mentioned, that's actually technically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 75.69,
          "end": 77.78999999999999,
          "en": "a feature built into React,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 77.78999999999999,
          "end": 80.64,
          "en": "but it must be unlocked, you could say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 80.64,
          "end": 82.77,
          "en": "with a certain behind the scenes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 82.77,
          "end": 84.93,
          "en": "build process and structure,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 84.93,
          "end": 87.66,
          "en": "that's not part of most React projects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 87.66,
          "end": 90.9,
          "en": "But it is unlocked and it is the standard",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 90.9,
          "end": 93.50999999999999,
          "en": "in NextJS projects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 93.50999999999999,
          "end": 96.81,
          "en": "Therefore, thereby default, all React components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 96.81,
          "end": 99.27000000000001,
          "en": "are such React Server components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 99.27000000000001,
          "end": 102.36,
          "en": "and are only rendered on the Server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 102.36,
          "end": 106.56,
          "en": "So that means that this component and this layout component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 106.56,
          "end": 109.95,
          "en": "but also the slideshow component at the header component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 109.95,
          "end": 113.25,
          "en": "all those components do not execute in the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 113.25,
          "end": 115.65,
          "en": "Those component functions don't execute there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 115.65,
          "end": 117.72,
          "en": "but instead on the Server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 117.72,
          "end": 119.85,
          "en": "And you can see that that's the case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 119.85,
          "end": 122.193,
          "en": "if you console log executing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 123.09,
          "end": 125.763,
          "en": "Here in this main header component, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 127.08,
          "end": 130.35,
          "en": "If you do that, and you then go to the page.js file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 130.35,
          "end": 132.75,
          "en": "and you temporarily comment out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 132.75,
          "end": 136.29,
          "en": "the image slideshow component since it's causing an error,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 136.29,
          "end": 137.79,
          "en": "which we'll fix soon,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 137.79,
          "end": 139.743,
          "en": "and you also comment out that import,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 140.97,
          "end": 144.75,
          "en": "you'll see that if you save everything and you reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 144.75,
          "end": 147.63,
          "en": "if you open your browser developer tools,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 147.63,
          "end": 151.47,
          "en": "you will not see that executing log here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 151.47,
          "end": 153.15,
          "en": "So that executing log,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 153.15,
          "end": 155.55,
          "en": "which we are logging in the main header,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 155.55,
          "end": 157.17000000000002,
          "en": "it's not showing up here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 157.17000000000002,
          "end": 159.57,
          "en": "because the main header component function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 159.57,
          "end": 161.823,
          "en": "never executes in the browser,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 163.62,
          "end": 166.5,
          "en": "instead, it executes on the Server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 166.5,
          "end": 168.99,
          "en": "And therefore if you open that terminal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 168.99,
          "end": 171.45,
          "en": "where you start the development Server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 171.45,
          "end": 174.66,
          "en": "which is running that Server side code, therefore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 174.66,
          "end": 177.513,
          "en": "you see those executing logs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 178.38,
          "end": 181.323,
          "en": "So, it's there where those components execute.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 182.4,
          "end": 186.51,
          "en": "And what's interesting, is that this is not just the case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 186.51,
          "end": 188.4,
          "en": "for the initial page load,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 188.4,
          "end": 191.73,
          "en": "but also for subsequent navigations.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 191.73,
          "end": 195.66,
          "en": "So if I, for example, also log something on that meals page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 195.66,
          "end": 198.333,
          "en": "if I console log meals page here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 199.71,
          "end": 202.59,
          "en": "and I then reload the starting page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 202.59,
          "end": 206.37,
          "en": "and I click on explore meals to be taken to that meals page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 206.37,
          "end": 208.71,
          "en": "I don't see that log here either,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 208.71,
          "end": 210.84,
          "en": "even though I used that link",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 210.84,
          "end": 215.34,
          "en": "and we therefore stayed in that single page application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 215.34,
          "end": 218.46,
          "en": "we did not fetch a brand new page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 218.46,
          "end": 222.24,
          "en": "But even though that's the case, I don't see the log here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 222.24,
          "end": 225.213,
          "en": "instead I see it here in that backend log.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 226.17000000000002,
          "end": 228.87,
          "en": "And that's happening, because even if you are",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 228.87,
          "end": 230.91,
          "en": "in that single page application mode",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 230.91,
          "end": 232.59,
          "en": "and you're navigating around,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 232.59,
          "end": 235.8,
          "en": "all the components will still be rendered on the Server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 235.8,
          "end": 237.48,
          "en": "on the backend, and in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 237.48,
          "end": 240.33,
          "en": "it's kind of the finished HTML code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 240.33,
          "end": 243.39,
          "en": "that's then sent to the client to be rendered there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 243.39,
          "end": 245.19,
          "en": "It's technically a bit different,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 245.19,
          "end": 247.41,
          "en": "but that is how you can think about it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 247.41,
          "end": 250.47,
          "en": "And therefore NextJS embraces this concept",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 250.47,
          "end": 253.65,
          "en": "of having those Server components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 253.65,
          "end": 255.75,
          "en": "Now that's an important concept",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 255.75,
          "end": 260.07,
          "en": "and an important advantage of NextJS projects,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 260.07,
          "end": 262.44,
          "en": "because with Server components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 262.44,
          "end": 266.28,
          "en": "you have potentially less client side JavaScript code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 266.28,
          "end": 268.29,
          "en": "that must be downloaded,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 268.29,
          "end": 272.31,
          "en": "hence possibly improving the performance of your website.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 272.31,
          "end": 276.3,
          "en": "And it's also great for search engine optimization,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 276.3,
          "end": 280.23,
          "en": "because web search crawlers now see pages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 280.23,
          "end": 284.19,
          "en": "that contain the complete finished content.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 284.19,
          "end": 287.25,
          "en": "Compare that with a Vanilla JavaScript project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 287.25,
          "end": 290.94,
          "en": "where you are not using a framework like NextJS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 290.94,
          "end": 294.78,
          "en": "There, if you take a look at the source code of a page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 294.78,
          "end": 297.48,
          "en": "you'll see that it's essentially an empty page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 297.48,
          "end": 299.61,
          "en": "because all the content is created",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 299.61,
          "end": 303.15,
          "en": "and populated on the client side by client side code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 303.15,
          "end": 306.09,
          "en": "with help of those client side components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 306.09,
          "end": 308.85,
          "en": "In NextJS, project stats different.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 308.85,
          "end": 311.79,
          "en": "If you take a look at the source code there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 311.79,
          "end": 314.28,
          "en": "you will see that all the content is in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 314.28,
          "end": 317.07,
          "en": "All that text that's visible on the screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 317.07,
          "end": 320.16,
          "en": "is part of the actual page source code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 320.16,
          "end": 324.15,
          "en": "and that is also what web search engine crawlers will see.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 324.15,
          "end": 327.48,
          "en": "So that's why we have this concept of Server components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 327.48,
          "end": 329.433,
          "en": "and why it's an important concept.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 330.42,
          "end": 333.24,
          "en": "Nonetheless, in NextJS projects,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 333.24,
          "end": 336.87,
          "en": "you can still also build client components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 336.87,
          "end": 338.37,
          "en": "and that would be components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 338.37,
          "end": 342.24,
          "en": "that are still technically pre-rendered on the server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 342.24,
          "end": 346.35,
          "en": "but then also potentially rendered on the client.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 346.35,
          "end": 349.17,
          "en": "And most importantly, these are components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 349.17,
          "end": 351.87,
          "en": "that must be rendered on the client",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 351.87,
          "end": 353.76,
          "en": "because they contain some code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 353.76,
          "end": 358.76,
          "en": "or use some features that are only available on the client.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 359.64,
          "end": 364.02,
          "en": "Like for example here in this image slideshow JS file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 364.02,
          "end": 367.263,
          "en": "they use state hook, or the use fact hook.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 368.1,
          "end": 372.63,
          "en": "These hooks are not available on the Server side,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 372.63,
          "end": 375.69,
          "en": "which kind of makes sense if you think about it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 375.69,
          "end": 379.29,
          "en": "because we're not interested in setting this interval",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 379.29,
          "end": 382.86,
          "en": "on the Server side, we wanna run this in the browser",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 382.86,
          "end": 385.71,
          "en": "so that the image swaps every five seconds",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 385.71,
          "end": 387.453,
          "en": "after the page has been loaded.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 388.8,
          "end": 390.75,
          "en": "Another example for a feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 390.75,
          "end": 393.6,
          "en": "that would only be available in client components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 393.6,
          "end": 395.61,
          "en": "would be event handlers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 395.61,
          "end": 397.59000000000003,
          "en": "So if you would use the on click prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 397.59000000000003,
          "end": 399.65999999999997,
          "en": "to trigger some function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 399.65999999999997,
          "end": 401.46,
          "en": "obviously since you are waiting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 401.46,
          "end": 403.47,
          "en": "for some user interaction here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 403.47,
          "end": 406.2,
          "en": "that would require to be a client component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
          "start": 406.2,
          "end": 409.95,
          "en": "because that would require code that runs on the client.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 137,
          "start": 409.95,
          "end": 412.98,
          "en": "But since by default in NextJS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 138,
          "start": 412.98,
          "end": 415.59000000000003,
          "en": "all components are Server components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 139,
          "start": 415.59000000000003,
          "end": 418.62,
          "en": "You have to explicitly tell NextJS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 140,
          "start": 418.62,
          "end": 420.9,
          "en": "if you wanna build a client component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 141,
          "start": 420.9,
          "end": 424.14,
          "en": "by using a special directive at the top of the file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 142,
          "start": 424.14,
